epend on could it be better  absolutely but tearing it down or  destabilizing it doesn't benefit anybody  and there are a lot of people whose  family's well-being you know my  partner's mother just to give you an  example she relies on this tuba cream  it's actually chemotherapy for skin  cancer her life depends on this stuff it  would be two three thousand bucks per  month if she didn't have coverage  through the ACA this is about real  people in their daily lives and that's  what the stakes really are for all of us  let's talk about trade and jobs  manufacturing jobs in America have been  going down is there something that can  be done about that and what impact does  trade have on that which seems to be the  mantra of a president Trump well we need  to understand that you can't unglue  belies the world and you can't turn back  the clock on technology what you can do  is create a reality where technology and  trade are a situation where workers have  a place in the economic story other than  that of victim right now in South Bend  we've got workers union auto workers who  are working on a line with a contract  assembly making Mercedes vehicles that  are sold to Chinese customers so we got  American Union Auto Workers making  German cars going to Asian markets  shipping the goods not the jobs to Asia  workers can win in today's economy but  it's not going to happen by turning back  the clock you don't want to start a  trade war but does the president have a  point in which he says there's a lot of  unfair trade agreements in place that  hurt American workers well certainly the  case that American workers feel that  they've been treated unfairly and that's  not just because of trade but are they  right they've been treated unfairly I  think that it's easy to blame trade when  technology has changed a lot of things  but yes workers are being treated  unfairly among other things workers are  being treated unfairly by financial  institutions that are jerking us around  I think the president would rather we  not pay attention to that as he works to  put even less restriction on the way  Wall Street behaves but I think that's  where the action is if you want to make  families better off we come into a point  in which we have to redefine work I  think we might be I mean certainly  technology is changing things profoundly  think about this right now we're  basically at what economists would call  full employment and yet we just had an  election that's a kind of election you'd  have in conditions of intense economic  anxiety how can you have economic  anxiety and most people working at the  same time well means there's more to  jobs than just the unemployment rate or  whether you have one or not let's talk  about you you're 34 years old 35 now 30  35 a degree from Harvard and Oxford you  were a Rhodes Scholar worked as a and  currently a Navy reservist what's in  your a Democrat what's wrong with the  Democratic Party well I think we're  tying ourselves up in knots over what  our message is going to be and sometimes  falling into the trap of the  it's it's all about Russia or it's all  about opposition when the thing that  Democrats in my view have always been  about at least the reason I'm a Democrat  is that we're a party that exists to  defend and support ordinary people going  about their lives I think that's a  powerful message and I think we've got a  lot more going for us as a party than we  think if we give back to our values and  get back to our message so what happened  why did you need to get back your  message and get back and get back to  something what happened to the  Democratic Party so that it lost that so  that in the 2016 election people didn't  think of the Democratic Party that way I  think much focused on identity politics  and it was too much focused on  Washington you know this show has become  so mesmerizing even more so since the  election because it's so twisted we  can't take our eyes off it and so we're  talking about what's going on in the  capital without remembering that the  only reason any of that even matters is  what those decisions do to people in  places like South Beth and Democrats  used to be very good at talking about  that but now we're so consumed with  who's up and who's down and what's  happening in this committee and the  Russia and believe me I get that that  matters but look even if this  investigation leads to a new president  it doesn't change the fact that only  four in ten Americans currently believe  that Democrats are for something they've  got to know what were for not just what  we're against you're a progressive  Democrat in a state that Donald Trump  won by double digits  it's former governors now the country's  vice president what are some ways that  you can work together with Republicans  on because it does seem like that's what  this country is craving well that's one  of the great things about being a mayor  in fact right now I'm here because  Bloomberg philanthropies is convened 40  mayor's from around the world in a  partnership with Harvard to help us all  get better at our jobs and their mayors  I've gotten to know and like to be  honest I'd have to go back and look it  up whether they're Republicans or  Democrats that's not how we think we're  in charge of delivery and I think when  you keep the focus on results when  you're picking up the trash filling in  the holes in the road and working to  create jobs people give you a lot of  credit whether you're from the same  party as they are or not and I'll work  with anybody who can help us do that  because it's not always about ideology  is any reason to believe that an  American with the experience and who  talks about economics and foreign policy  cannot be elected because he or she is  gay  I don't know it's not for me to say but  but what I will say is that when I came  out in a socially conservative community  like South Bend I got reelected with 80%  of the vote I think people don't really  care it's the same as when I was in the  military you know when when I got into a  vehicle that I was responsible for  driving or guarding the people who got  in the vehicle with me they want to know  if I'd read the Intel reports on where  the IEDs might be they want to know if  I'd chambered around in my m4 and if I  knew how to use it they didn't care  whether I was a Democrat or Republican  whether my father did was yeah or  whether I was going home to a boyfriend  or girlfriend  they just cared whether they could trust  me with their lives and I think it's the  same relationship people have to their  mayors and their political leaders well  may I keep her coming thank you so much  for coming by I appreciate it mayor  Budaj
 

